Creating an AudioComponent to Associate
Actors with Sound Events
The premise behind an AudioComponent class is to associate sound events with specific actors.
This way, when the actor moves, AudioComponent can update the associated event’s 3D
attributes. Furthermore, if an actor dies, any sound events associated with the actor can stop.
Listing 7.8 gives the declaration of AudioComponent. Note that it has two different
std::vector collections: one for 2D events and one for 3D events. The only member
functions not inherited from Component are PlayEvent and StopAllEvents.
